IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `cbr-nouns`

-- Child Benefit (Rates) Regulations 2006 -- LAYER 1, MODULE 3: REGULATION 2(6)
-- (the specified benefits) AND REGULATION 2(5) (the enhanced rate where a specified
-- benefit is paid).
--
-- Why these two together: paragraph (5) uses "specified benefit" and paragraph (6)
-- defines it, and nothing else in regulation 2 reads either.
--
-- Out of text (NOTES.md, "Dependencies"): the Table in Part 4 of Schedule 4 to SSCBA
-- and Part IV of Schedule 4 to SSCB(NI)A. Whether "receipt of which entitles the
-- recipient to an increase specified in column 2" holds is asked as a fact.
-- A judgment the text hands to the Commissioners for Her Majesty's Revenue and
-- Customs (sub-paragraph (c)(viii)) is a conditional input, never guessed.

§ `Regulation 2(5) and (6): specified benefits`

§§ `Regulation 2(6): the benefits that are specified benefits`

-- src:39 | (6) The following are specified benefits—
-- src:40 | (a) any benefit under SSCBA receipt of which entitles the recipient to an increase specified in column 2 of the Table in Part 4 of Schedule 4 to that Act (increases for dependants);
@ref reg 2(6)(a) (src:39-40)
GIVEN payment IS A `Payment made for the week`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a payment is a specified benefit under paragraph (6)(a)` payment MEANS
        (payment's `kind of payment` EQUALS `a benefit under SSCBA`)
    AND payment's `receipt of the benefit entitles the recipient to an increase for dependants specified in the Table in Schedule 4 to that Act`

-- src:41 | (b) any benefit under SSCB (NI) A receipt of which entitles the recipient to an increase specified in column 2 of the Table in Part IV of Schedule 4 to that Act (increases for dependants in Northern Ireland);
@ref reg 2(6)(b) (src:41)
GIVEN payment IS A `Payment made for the week`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a payment is a specified benefit under paragraph (6)(b)` payment MEANS
        (payment's `kind of payment` EQUALS `a benefit under SSCB(NI)A`)
    AND payment's `receipt of the benefit entitles the recipient to an increase for dependants specified in the Table in Schedule 4 to that Act`

-- src:42 | (c) an allowance for a child or a qualifying young person granted in respect of the death of a person due to service or war injury—
-- src:43 | (i) under the Armed Forces and Reserve Forces (Compensation Scheme) Order 2005;
-- src:44 | (ii) under the Naval, Military and Air Forces Etc. (Disablement and Death) Service Pensions Order 1983;
-- src:45 | (iii) under the Pensions (Polish Forces) Scheme 1964;
-- src:46 | (iv) under the War Pensions (Mercantile Marine) Scheme 1964;
-- src:47 | (v) under the Warrant of 21 st December 1964 concerning pensions and grants in respect of disablement or death due to service in the Home Guard;
-- src:48 | (vi) under the Order of 22 nd December 1964 concerning pensions and grants in respect of disablement or death due to service in the Home Guard after 27 th April 1952;
-- src:49 | (vii) under the Order by Her Majesty dated 4 th January 1971 in respect of service in the Ulster Defence Regiment; or
@ref reg 2(6)(c)(i) to (vii) (src:42-49)
GIVEN instrument IS AN `Instrument granting an allowance for a child on a death due to service or war injury`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`an instrument is one of those listed in paragraph (6)(c)(i) to (vii)` instrument MEANS
    CONSIDER instrument
    WHEN `the Armed Forces and Reserve Forces (Compensation Scheme) Order 2005` THEN TRUE                                -- (i)
    WHEN `the Naval, Military and Air Forces Etc. (Disablement and Death) Service Pensions Order 1983` THEN TRUE         -- (ii)
    WHEN `the Pensions (Polish Forces) Scheme 1964` THEN TRUE                                                            -- (iii)
    WHEN `the War Pensions (Mercantile Marine) Scheme 1964` THEN TRUE                                                    -- (iv)
    WHEN `the Warrant of 21st December 1964 concerning pensions and grants in respect of disablement or death due to service in the Home Guard` THEN TRUE   -- (v)
    WHEN `the Order of 22nd December 1964 concerning pensions and grants in respect of disablement or death due to service in the Home Guard after 27th April 1952` THEN TRUE   -- (vi)
    WHEN `the Order by Her Majesty dated 4th January 1971 in respect of service in the Ulster Defence Regiment` THEN TRUE   -- (vii)
    WHEN `an instrument not listed in paragraph (6)(c)(i) to (vii)` THEN FALSE

-- src:42 | (c) an allowance for a child or a qualifying young person granted in respect of the death of a person due to service or war injury—
-- src:43 | (i) under the Armed Forces and Reserve Forces (Compensation Scheme) Order 2005;
-- src:44 | (ii) under the Naval, Military and Air Forces Etc. (Disablement and Death) Service Pensions Order 1983;
-- src:45 | (iii) under the Pensions (Polish Forces) Scheme 1964;
-- src:46 | (iv) under the War Pensions (Mercantile Marine) Scheme 1964;
-- src:47 | (v) under the Warrant of 21 st December 1964 concerning pensions and grants in respect of disablement or death due to service in the Home Guard;
-- src:48 | (vi) under the Order of 22 nd December 1964 concerning pensions and grants in respect of disablement or death due to service in the Home Guard after 27 th April 1952;
-- src:49 | (vii) under the Order by Her Majesty dated 4 th January 1971 in respect of service in the Ulster Defence Regiment; or
@ref reg 2(6)(c)(i) to (vii) (src:42-49)
GIVEN payment IS A `Payment made for the week`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a payment is a specified benefit under paragraph (6)(c)(i) to (vii)` payment MEANS
        (payment's `kind of payment` EQUALS `an allowance for a child or a qualifying young person granted in respect of the death of a person due to service or war injury`)
    AND `an instrument is one of those listed in paragraph (6)(c)(i) to (vii)` (payment's `instrument granting the allowance`)

-- src:50 | (viii) which the Commissioners for Her Majesty's Revenue and Customs accept as being analogous to an allowance for a child granted in respect of the death of a person due to service or war injury under any of the preceding provisions of this sub-paragraph.
@ref reg 2(6)(c)(viii) (src:50)
GIVEN payment IS A `Payment made for the week`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a payment is a specified benefit under paragraph (6)(c)(viii)` payment MEANS
        (payment's `kind of payment` EQUALS `an allowance for a child or a qualifying young person granted in respect of the death of a person due to service or war injury`)
    AND payment's `the Commissioners accept the allowance as analogous to one granted under those instruments`

-- src:39 | (6) The following are specified benefits—
@ref reg 2(6) (src:39)
GIVEN payment IS A `Payment made for the week`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a payment is a specified benefit` payment MEANS
        `a payment is a specified benefit under paragraph (6)(a)` payment
    OR  `a payment is a specified benefit under paragraph (6)(b)` payment
    OR  `a payment is a specified benefit under paragraph (6)(c)(i) to (vii)` payment
    OR  `a payment is a specified benefit under paragraph (6)(c)(viii)` payment

§§ `Regulation 2(5): the enhanced rate where a specified benefit is paid`

-- "which is a specified benefit": read as qualifying the allowance, or the benefit,
-- pension or allowance of which there is an increase (fork F6). Limbs (a) and (b)
-- are cumulative; the whole sentence is the condition for the closing words.
-- Whether this paragraph or paragraph (4) prevails where both apply is NOT said by
-- the text: fork F1.
-- src:35 | (5) If an allowance, or an increase of a benefit, pension or allowance, which is a specified benefit, is paid in respect of a week—
-- src:36 | (a) to a person, and
-- src:37 | (b) in respect of the only, elder or eldest child or qualifying young person in respect of whom that person is entitled to child benefit,
-- src:38 | child benefit shall be payable at the enhanced rate for that week.
@ref reg 2(5) (src:35-38)
GIVEN payment IS A `Payment made for the week`
      child IS A `Child or qualifying young person at the start of the week`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`paragraph (5) gives the enhanced rate for the child` payment child MEANS
        `a payment is a specified benefit` payment
    AND payment's `paid to the claimant in respect of the week`                                  -- (a)
    AND payment's `paid in respect of the child or qualifying young person`                      -- (b)
    AND child's `the only person, or the elder or eldest person, in respect of whom child benefit is payable to the claimant`   -- (b)
